<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan to invest C$750,000 in canola mill.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan to invest C$750,000 in canola mill.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan Agriculture Minister Eric Upshall said Friday that provincial Agri-Food Equity Fund will invest C$750,000 to help build a canola mill.</p>
<p>Lloydminster-based EXL Milling Inc plans to process low-grade canola and canola meal into a high quality livestock feed, according to a Saskatchewan Agriculture statement.</p>
<p>EXL plans to produce at least 10,000 tonnes of product each year for sale to the domestic and international markets. A pilot project four years ago showed interest in the product.</p>
<p>&quot;Our product, MegaPro, has been very well received across Canada and much of the U.S,&quot; EXL president Sydney Palmer said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
